A||N||14||Slapnutz2000||Question about exhaust... ||||5||
Z||000000||Slapnutz2000||06-30-2000||02:43 PM||||This might be a silly question but I get a puff of smoke out of my exhaust after I idle at a stoplight. Is there a problem I should know about or is this normal? (1986 2m4 automatic with 73,350 miles) <P>I had a 1996 Accord before my Fiero and it never happen with that car so...<P>TIA!||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||07-02-2000||11:23 AM||||what color smoke?<P>no. it's not normal. likely the motor is gettting worn if it's oil(blue/white) or there is s fuel system problem (black smoke.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||07-02-2000||02:27 PM||||If the smoke is blue its oil. If it’s black it’s a fuel problem. If you get this puff when you start your engine after it sat for a long time then chances are it's valve guide seals. If your plugs get a sticky oily substance on the electrode in a very short time and your engine spews blue smoke all the time especially on deceleration than chances are it's a oil ring sealing problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slapnutz2000||07-02-2000||05:25 PM||||The smoke is whitish gray...looks like smoke.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000004||hugh||07-02-2000||06:45 PM||||when your engine is idling your manifold vacuum is greater and can draw some oil down the valve guides.It probably smokes on a cold startup too.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Slapnutz2000||07-03-2000||06:39 PM||||Is this something I should be concerned about or is it just normal for a car that age?||||reg||5
Z||000006||hugh||07-03-2000||09:20 PM||||I wouldn't be concerned unless it smokes all the time,or too much too long,or fouls spark plugs.If it only does it off idle or cold start up.I wouldn'tworry about it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fret Naught||07-03-2000||11:30 PM||||I vote for worn valve guides, pretty normal on worn engines, I wouldn't worry about it to much, just check your oil to make sure it doesn't get low and add that to your mental list of reasons "why I need to re-build/replace my engine with something bigger and better"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slapnutz2000||07-04-2000||12:58 AM||||How much would it cost to fix the worn valve guides?||||reg||5
Z||000009||Fret Naught||07-04-2000||01:00 PM||||Well, here is the thing, it is just my opinion, and I would most certainly get lots of input before you proceed.<P>You have to pull the heads, to replace valve guides, and while you have gone to all that trouble you might as well take the heads in and have a complete valve job done. so now you got about I don't know whats a Valve job running these days about 3 maybe 4 hundred?<BR>(My buddy does Valve jobs, I do electrical work we trade labor, so I haven't paid for one in years)<BR>So you get it all done, new gaskets etc... put it together, and you have a new top end, but your lower end is still wore. What condition is it in? are the rings wore? cylinder walls in good shape? What about bearings see what I am driving at? That is why I said I wouldn't worry about it to much until I was ready to do the whole thing. It could be that six months after you are done you will need to tear it all down again. I can't stress enough that this is just my opinion, I am sort of anal in this area, I figure if I am going to do then Lets wait until it all has to be done and do it in one shot.  That way you know for certain what you have from the ground up.||||reg||7
Z||000010||fldevel||07-04-2000||01:19 PM||||Time for a V6!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||07-04-2000||02:53 PM||||Just get another rebuilt head from the Fiero Store and replace the head if it’s the valve guides. The Iron Dukes are easy to do by comparison to the v6. The four cylinders are notorious for bad valve guide seals. You can also replace the seals without removing the head if you want to be cheap. Just get a good repair manual and do it. <P>Don’t waste your time and money rebuilding the engine if it dose not need a rebuild.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Slapnutz2000||07-04-2000||03:25 PM||||I got a valve job, replaced the heads, put on a new head gasket, and changed the oil and transmission fluid about 1350 miles ago. Could this just be the process of breaking everything back in.<P>The car runs fine but rumbles a little around 30 MPH...I think that's about 2nd gear on my automatic.||||reg||14
Z||000013||webbee||07-04-2000||06:59 PM||||Compression test time. Then you'll know if it's the bottom end. How many mi. on the engine?||||reg||1
Z||000014||ThatRickGuy||07-05-2000||01:08 PM||||I'd go with Fred on this one. Most engine shops will really urge you to do the same, part because they get money out of it, and part because they don't want you to drive 2 miles, throw a rod, and blame them. Out here on the east coast my engine rebuild (Hot tank, bore, balance, new pistons and all etc...) is going to run $900-$1400, but labor our here is rather expencive, back in the midwest I would be looking at arround $900 tops. For a bigger, beter, warrentied engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
